"""Focused T14 block checks; never launches a performance-core ISA sweep."""
import argparse
import hashlib
import json
from pathlib import Path
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]

def assertion_names(count):
    return ('assert__chisel3_builtin',) + tuple(f'assert__chisel3_builtin_{i}' for i in range(count-1))


# Reviewed authorization-to-property bindings. The integrity digest prevents
# reordered autogenerated labels silently moving a deferral to another check.
# A harness change requires review of this mapping; this is not an RTL test.
PROPERTY_BINDINGS = {
    'bus': ('hw/ip/bus/formal/BusFormal.scala',
            'a5fe33e37f64b53a2a60b8275b64e1143e4a38156c0a6f1f2a077ec58d3e8edb'),
    'bus_bridge': ('hw/ip/bus_bridge/formal/BridgeFormal.scala',
                   '0b4d1466dfe0818dc5e541e434ae4ba6d70eea8d6c05151f420ab4862c5baf05'),
}
DEFERRED = {
    'bus': tuple((f'T14-BUS-FAIR-M{i}', prop) for i, prop in enumerate(assertion_names(34)[:3])),
    'bus_bridge': (('T14-BRIDGE-RETURN-DATA', 'assert__chisel3_builtin_6'),),
}
FAULT_PROPERTIES = {
    'bus': frozenset(f'assert__chisel3_builtin_{i}' for i in (10,14,18)),
    'bus_bridge': frozenset(('assert__chisel3_builtin_6',)),
}
SUCCESS = frozenset(('pass', 'pass_with_deferrals'))


def approved_plan(block):
    if block not in DEFERRED:
        raise ValueError('No authorized partition plan for this block')
    full = assertion_names(34 if block == 'bus' else 14)
    groups = ({'protocol': full[3:]} if block == 'bus' else
              {'source_dispatch': full[:3], 'target_dispatch': full[3:5],
               'control': tuple(p for p in full[5:] if p != 'assert__chisel3_builtin_6')})
    plan = dict(block=block, full=full, deferred=DEFERRED[block], groups=groups)
    validate_plan(plan)
    return plan


def validate_plan(plan):
    block = plan['block']
    expected = assertion_names({'bus':34, 'bus_bridge':14}[block])
    if tuple(plan['full']) != expected or tuple(plan['deferred']) != DEFERRED[block]:
        raise ValueError('Property identities or authorized deferrals changed')
    flat = [p for group in plan['groups'].values() for p in group]
    if (not all(plan['groups'].values()) or len(flat) != len(set(flat)) or
            set(flat) != set(expected) - {p for _,p in DEFERRED[block]}):
        raise ValueError('Active groups must cover the exact authorized remainder once')


def validate_binding(block, content):
    actual = hashlib.sha256(content.replace(b'\r\n', b'\n')).hexdigest()
    if actual != PROPERTY_BINDINGS[block][1]:
        raise ValueError('Formal harness changed; review identities before applying deferrals')
    return actual


def property_guards(kind, names):
    return [f'select -assert-count {len(names)} t:$'+kind] + [
        'select -assert-count 1 t:$'+kind+f' c:{name} %i' for name in names]


def proof_selection(plan, group):
    validate_plan(plan)
    keep = plan['groups'][group]
    remove = [p for p in plan['full'] if p not in keep]
    return property_guards('assert', plan['full']) + [
        'chformal -assert -remove ' + ' '.join('c:'+p for p in remove),
        'opt_clean -purge'] + property_guards('assert', keep)


def concrete_witnesses(directory):
    return [p for p in directory.glob('engine_*/trace*.vcd')
            if not p.name.startswith('trace_induct') and '$enddefinitions' in p.read_text()
            and re.search(r'^#\d+', p.read_text(), re.M)]


def fault_identities(directory):
    """Read counterexample metadata; BTOR witnesses use a numbered bad property."""
    log = (directory/'logfile.txt').read_text()
    found = set(re.findall(r'failed assertion [\w.]+\.(assert__\w+)', log))
    found.update(re.findall(r'Assert failed in [\w.]+: (assert__\w+)', log))
    model = directory/'model/design_btor.btor'
    if model.exists():
        names = re.findall(r'^\d+ bad \d+ (\S+)', model.read_text(), re.M)
        for witness in directory.glob('engine_*/trace*.wit'):
            text = witness.read_text()
            if not text.startswith('sat\n') or '#0' not in text:
                continue
            for number in re.findall(r'\bb(\d+)\b', text.split('#0',1)[0]):
                index = int(number)
                if index >= len(names):
                    raise ValueError('Fault witness references unknown property')
                found.add(names[index])
    return found


def validate_job(directory, mode, code, status, expected_faults=None):
    negative = mode == 'negative'
    if status != ('FAIL' if negative else 'PASS') or code != (2 if negative else 0):
        raise RuntimeError(f'{directory.name}: {status}')
    if mode in ('cover','negative') and not concrete_witnesses(directory):
        raise RuntimeError('No concrete counterexample/cover witness')
    if negative and expected_faults is not None:
        failures = fault_identities(directory)
        if not failures or not failures <= expected_faults:
            raise RuntimeError(f'Negative control failed unexpected properties: {sorted(failures)}')
        return sorted(failures)
    return []


def gate_status(required, outcomes, has_deferrals):
    if set(required) != set(outcomes) or any(outcomes[j] != 'pass' for j in required):
        raise RuntimeError('Every required active proof, cover and fault job must pass')
    return 'pass_with_deferrals' if has_deferrals else 'pass'


def prove_block(name,top,emitter,output,assertions,covers,extra=(),multiclock=False,resets=('reset_n',),depth=64,assumptions=(),cover_engines='smtbmc z3',negative_engines=None,partitioned=False):
    output.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    receipt=dict(block=name,status='running',runs=[],timeout_seconds=120,cover_depth=depth,
                 assumptions=[f'initial {r}=0, subsequently arbitrary' for r in resets]+list(assumptions),
                 engine='abc pdr',cover_engines=cover_engines.splitlines(),negative_engines=negative_engines,
                 assertions=assertions,covers=covers,
                 configuration=list(extra),scope='unbounded safety; finite cover witnesses; actual RTL fault',
                 deferred=[],qualification_limits=[])
    start=time.monotonic()
    def command(cmd,label,timeout=180):
        before=time.monotonic()
        with (output/(label+'.log')).open('w') as stream:
            p=subprocess.run(cmd,cwd=ROOT,stdout=stream,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,timeout=timeout)
        receipt['runs'].append(dict(command=cmd,returncode=p.returncode,seconds=time.monotonic()-before,log=label+'.log'))
        return p.returncode
    try:
        plan=approved_plan(name) if partitioned else None
        if plan:
            if len(plan['full'])!=assertions:raise ValueError('Assertion count disagrees with property map')
            source,digest=PROPERTY_BINDINGS[name]
            validate_binding(name,(ROOT/source).read_bytes())
            receipt['property_binding']=dict(source=source,sha256=digest,properties=plan['full'])
            receipt['deferred']=[dict(id=ident,block=name,property=prop,status='deferred_unproved',
                authorization='User decision 2026-11-17') for ident,prop in plan['deferred']]
            receipt['active_groups']=plan['groups']
            receipt['active_assertions']=sum(map(len,plan['groups'].values()))
            receipt['scope']='Authorized active proof gate; listed deferred properties remain unproved'
            if name=='bus_bridge':
                receipt['qualification_limits']=['Bridge proof watchdog is 32; production default is 131072.']
        args=' '.join([*extra,str(output/'emit')])
        if command([sys.executable,'tools/sbt.py',f'hw/runMain {emitter} {args}'],'emit',600):raise RuntimeError('Emission failed')
        groups=list(plan['groups']) if plan else [None]
        jobs=[('cover','cover',None),('corrupt','corrupt',None)]+[
            ('correct_'+g if g else 'correct','correct',g) for g in groups]
        outcomes={}
        for label,variant,group in jobs:
            sources=sorted((output/'emit'/variant).glob('*.sv'))
            if not sources:raise RuntimeError('Missing source')
            cover=variant=='cover';negative=variant=='corrupt'
            cfg=output/(label+'.sby')
            mode='cover' if cover else ('bmc' if negative and negative_engines else 'prove')
            engine=cover_engines if cover else (negative_engines if negative and negative_engines else 'abc pdr')
            if group and name=='bus_bridge':engine='abc pdr\naiger suprove\nsmtbmc yices'
            guards=[f"select -assert-count {covers if cover else assertions} t:"+('$cover' if cover else '$assert')]
            if plan:
                names=('cover__cover',)+tuple(f'cover__cover_{i}' for i in range(1,covers))
                guards=(property_guards('cover',names) if cover else
                        proof_selection(plan,group) if group else property_guards('assert',plan['full']))
                if not cover:
                    guards += [f"select -assert-count {5 if name=='bus_bridge' else 16} t:$assume"]
            cfg.write_text('\n'.join(['[options]','mode '+mode,f'depth {depth}','timeout 120',*(['multiclock on'] if multiclock else []),'',
                '[engines]',engine,'',
                '[script]',f'read_slang --top {top} '+' '.join(p.name for p in sources),f'prep -top {top} -flatten',
                'fminit '+' '.join(f"-seq {r} 0,'z" for r in resets),'clk2fflogic' if multiclock else 'async2sync','chformal -lower',
                *guards,'',
                '[files]',*map(str,sources),'']))
            code=command(['sby','-d',str(output/label),str(cfg)],label)
            status=(output/label/'status').read_text().split()[0] if (output/label/'status').exists() else 'ERROR'
            receipt['runs'][-1]['status']=status
            failures=validate_job(output/label,'cover' if cover else 'negative' if negative else 'proof',
                                  code,status,FAULT_PROPERTIES.get(name) if plan else None)
            if failures:receipt['runs'][-1]['failed_properties']=failures
            outcomes[label]='pass'
            print(f'PASS {name} {label}: {status}',flush=True)
        receipt['status']=gate_status([j[0] for j in jobs],outcomes,bool(receipt['deferred']))
    except Exception as e:
        receipt.update(status='unresolved' if 'TIMEOUT' in str(e) or isinstance(e,subprocess.TimeoutExpired) else 'failed',error=str(e));print(f'{name}: {e}',flush=True)
    finally:
        receipt['seconds']=time.monotonic()-start
        (output/'result.json').write_text(json.dumps(receipt,indent=2)+'\n')
    return receipt


def main():
    ap=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
    ap.add_argument('--blocks',required=True);ap.add_argument('--output',required=True)
    args=ap.parse_args();blocks=args.blocks.split(',')
    if not set(blocks)<={'cdc','bus','bus_bridge','mailbox'}:ap.error('Unknown block')
    if ('bus_bridge' in blocks or 'mailbox' in blocks) and 'cdc' not in blocks:
        blocks.insert(0,'cdc')
    out=(ROOT/args.output).resolve();out.relative_to(ROOT/'build')
    if (out/'result.json').exists():raise ValueError('Use fresh output; retain evidence')
    out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    def sources_snapshot():
        sources=[p for parent in ('hw/lib','hw/ip/bus','hw/ip/bus_bridge','hw/ip/mailbox') for p in (ROOT/parent).rglob('*') if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ('.scala','.py','.yaml')]+[Path(__file__),ROOT/'tools/test_formal.py',ROOT/'build.sbt']
        return {str(p.relative_to(ROOT)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in sources}
    snapshot=sources_snapshot()
    receipt=dict(status='running',source_sha256=snapshot,blocks={},deferred=[],qualification_limits=[],
                 commit=subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],cwd=ROOT,text=True).strip())
    start=time.monotonic()
    def retain(name,detail):
        receipt['blocks'][name]=detail['status']
        receipt['deferred'].extend(detail.get('deferred',[]))
        receipt['qualification_limits'].extend(detail.get('qualification_limits',[]))
    def child(name,script):
        result=subprocess.run([sys.executable,script,'--output',str(out/name)],cwd=ROOT)
        detail=json.loads((out/name/'result.json').read_text())
        retain(name,detail)
        if result.returncode or detail['status'] not in SUCCESS:raise RuntimeError(f'{name}: {detail["status"]}')
    try:
        for block in blocks:
            if block=='cdc':
                for width in (32,33,72):
                    result=subprocess.run([sys.executable,'hw/lib/formal/cdc_proof.py','--width',str(width),'--output',str(out/f'cdc-{width}')],cwd=ROOT)
                    if result.returncode:
                        status=json.loads((out/f'cdc-{width}'/'result.json').read_text())['status']
                        raise RuntimeError(f'CDC{width}: {status}')
                receipt['blocks'][block]='pass'
            elif block=='bus':
                r=prove_block(block,'BusFormal','deadhorse.bus.EmitBusFormal',out/block,34,10,extra=('128',),depth=144,
                    assumptions=('request/payload held until grant','target accepts one credit, returns arbitrary delayed/error data; explicit cancellation establishes quiescence'),
                    cover_engines='smtbmc z3\nbtor btormc',partitioned=True)
                retain(block,r)
                if r['status'] not in SUCCESS:raise RuntimeError(f'{block}: {r["status"]}')
            elif block=='bus_bridge':
                child('direction_permit','hw/ip/bus_bridge/formal/direction_permit_proof.py')
                r=prove_block(block,'BridgeFormal','deadhorse.bus_bridge.EmitBridgeFormal',out/block,14,6,multiclock=True,resets=('sn','tn','en'),depth=128,
                    assumptions=('request/payload held until grant','target accepts one credit, arbitrary delayed/error reply and independent reset/cancellation','permit retained while request remains asserted; arbitrary grant delay'),
                    cover_engines='smtbmc z3\nsmtbmc yices\nsmtbmc bitwuzla\nbtor btormc',
                    negative_engines='smtbmc yices\nbtor btormc',partitioned=True)
                retain(block,r)
                if r['status'] not in SUCCESS:raise RuntimeError(f'{block}: {r["status"]}')
            else:child('mailbox','hw/ip/mailbox/formal/mailbox_proof.py')
        if snapshot!=sources_snapshot():raise RuntimeError('Sources changed during formal run')
        receipt['status']='pass_with_deferrals' if receipt['deferred'] else 'pass'
    except Exception as e:receipt.update(status='unresolved' if 'unresolved' in str(e) else 'failed',error=str(e));print(str(e),file=sys.stderr)
    finally:
        receipt['seconds']=time.monotonic()-start;(out/'result.json').write_text(json.dumps(receipt,indent=2)+'\n')
    print(f'{receipt["status"].upper()}: active formal gate; {len(receipt["deferred"])} deferred/unproved',flush=True)
    return 0 if receipt['status'] in SUCCESS else 1


if __name__=='__main__':sys.exit(main())
